 {:seon.task/name "a-tree-run-is-one-function"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the one-offs survey (the archived paper one-offs-2026-10-23.md (git history); owner, 2026-10-23: src resists growth so agents reuse and improve the core parts rather than making one-offs, DECISIONS). Item 5. What exists: seon.fx/build and seon.fx/run-tests repeat one mechanism (the env -u list, bin/worktree --at, a log file, a niced command in that tree, the cleanup), and test-results re-parses prove's stdout with regexes while seon.proofs holds each test's result by digest. Correct: one private in-tree runner both call, and run-tests reads seon.proofs' stored results instead of text. Proof: run-tests and seon.proofs agree on a red fixture. Risk: whether the stored results can be read from the child tree's results directory."
